evidence[8]:
  - Read both independent review0 artifacts; no new source discovery, runtime tests or product decisions needed.
  - P0-001 separates identification A, exact selector repair B and recursive deletion C. C retains all live marker/member/ancestor/containment premises including existing regular nonsymlink member; missing premise causes conservative refusal and retained membership. Saved receipt is not a substitute. V2/V3 cover recorded then missing or substituted paths and foreign selectors across layouts/retired.
  - P0-002 assigns command-specific lock roots, prune apply prefix-only and no writable bin/checkout requirement. T7 explicitly owns commands/prune.sh. Prune reads all claims/journals without recovery, protects pending releases after writer death and other-slot claims, and aborts on incomplete claims. V3/V6 include readonly bin0555/custom alias/checkout, concurrency and crash-pending-release-prune-retry with another slot.
  - P0-003 adds shared under-lock prior-journal normalization before every lifecycle batch including wrapper. Completed operations finalize membership before unrelated batch, unresolved journals remain protected and cannot be overwritten, partial known failure retains member and durable evidence without automatic deletion permission. V3 includes finalized uninstall crash then unrelated install then update plus completed-install analogue.
  - Plan0.2 has327 lines,28431 bytes;22 unique REQ rows,24 unique AC rows,7 task rows and18 valid source-relative local links. Growth is27 lines confined to required corrections and their tests/history.
  - Plan0.1 remains byte-identical at frozen hash. Review0 artifacts preserved; document check records their current hashes. Diff0.1-to0.2 confined to version, required technical corrections, corresponding owner/test edits and revision note.
  - Final tracked git diff empty; worktree only existing untracked dev/docs/history and specification. Future project plan and implementation-cycle history remain absent.
  - Binding remains effective prefix/bin pair; checkout locking for update does not bind state identity to checkout. No code/config/Git/host mutations, network, secrets, tests or implementation performed.
